.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn SSL_CTX_new_ex
creates a new
.Vt SSL_CTX
object, which holds various configuration and data relevant to SSL/TLS
or DTLS session establishment.
These are later inherited by the
.Sy SSL
object representing an active session.
The
.Fa method
parameter specifies whether the context will be used for the client or
server side or both - for details see the
.Sx NOTES
below.
The library context
.Fa libctx
(see
.Xr OSSL_LIB_CTX 3 )
is used to provide the cryptographic algorithms needed for the session.
Any cryptographic algorithms that are used by any
.Sy SSL
objects created from this
.Vt SSL_CTX
will be fetched from the
.Fa libctx
using the property query string
.Fa propq
(see
.Xr crypto 7 .
Either or both the
.Fa libctx
or
.Fa propq
parameters may be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_new
does the same as
.Fn SSL_CTX_new_ex
except that the default library context is used and no property query
string is specified.
.Pp
An
.Vt SSL_CTX
object is reference counted.
Creating an
.Vt SSL_CTX
object for the first time increments the reference count.
Freeing the
.Vt SSL_CTX
(using SSL_CTX_free) decrements it.
When the reference count drops to zero, any memory or resources
allocated to the
.Vt SSL_CTX
object are freed.
.Fn SSL_CTX_up_ref
increments the reference count for an existing
.Vt SSL_CTX
structure.
.Pp
An
.Vt SSL_CTX
object should not be changed after it is used to create any
.Sy SSL
objects or from multiple threads concurrently, since the implementation
does not provide serialization of access for these cases.
.Sh NOTES
On session establishment, by default, no peer credentials verification
is done.
This must be explicitly requested, typically using
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_verify 3 .
For verifying peer certificates many options can be set using various
functions such as
.Xr SSL_CTX_load_verify_locations 3
and
.Xr SSL_CTX_set1_param 3 .
.Pp
The SSL/(D)TLS implementation uses the
.Xr X509_STORE_CTX_set_default 3
function to prepare checks for
.Sy X509_PURPOSE_SSL_SERVER
on the client side and
.Sy X509_PURPOSE_SSL_CLIENT
on the server side.
The
.Xr X509_VERIFY_PARAM_set_purpose 3
function can be used, also in conjunction with
.Xr SSL_CTX_get0_param 3 ,
to override the default purpose of the session.
.Pp
The SSL_CTX object uses
.Fa method
as the connection method.
Three method variants are available: a generic method (for either client
or server use), a server-only method, and a client-only method.
.Pp
The
.Fa method
parameter of
.Fn SSL_CTX_new_ex
and
.Fn SSL_CTX_new
can be one of the following:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It TLS_method(), TLS_server_method(), TLS_client_method()
These are the general-purpose
.Em version-flexible
SSL/TLS methods.
The actual protocol version used will be negotiated to the highest
version mutually supported by the client and the server.
The supported protocols are SSLv3, TLSv1, TLSv1.1, TLSv1.2 and TLSv1.3.
Applications should use these methods, and avoid the version-specific
methods described below, which are deprecated.
.It SSLv23_method(), SSLv23_server_method(), SSLv23_client_method()
These functions do not exist anymore, they have been renamed to
.Fn TLS_method ,
.Fn TLS_server_method
and
.Fn TLS_client_method
respectively.
Currently, the old function calls are renamed to the corresponding new
ones by preprocessor macros, to ensure that existing code which uses the
old function names still compiles.
However, using the old function names is deprecated and new code should
call the new functions instead.
.It TLSv1_2_method(), TLSv1_2_server_method(), TLSv1_2_client_method()
A TLS/SSL connection established with these methods will only understand
the TLSv1.2 protocol.
These methods are deprecated.
.It TLSv1_1_method(), TLSv1_1_server_method(), TLSv1_1_client_method()
A TLS/SSL connection established with these methods will only understand
the TLSv1.1 protocol.
These methods are deprecated.
.It TLSv1_method(), TLSv1_server_method(), TLSv1_client_method()
A TLS/SSL connection established with these methods will only understand
the TLSv1 protocol.
These methods are deprecated.
.It SSLv3_method(), SSLv3_server_method(), SSLv3_client_method()
A TLS/SSL connection established with these methods will only understand
the SSLv3 protocol.
The SSLv3 protocol is deprecated and should not be used.
.It DTLS_method(), DTLS_server_method(), DTLS_client_method()
These are the version-flexible DTLS methods.
Currently supported protocols are DTLS 1.0 and DTLS 1.2.
.It DTLSv1_2_method(), DTLSv1_2_server_method(), DTLSv1_2_client_method()
These are the version-specific methods for DTLSv1.2. These methods are
deprecated.
.It DTLSv1_method(), DTLSv1_server_method(), DTLSv1_client_method()
These are the version-specific methods for DTLSv1. These methods are
deprecated.
.El
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_new
initializes the list of ciphers, the session cache setting, the
callbacks, the keys and certificates and the options to their default
values.
.Pp
.Fn TLS_method ,
.Fn TLS_server_method ,
.Fn TLS_client_method ,
.Fn DTLS_method ,
.Fn DTLS_server_method
and
.Fn DTLS_client_method
are the
.Em version-flexible
methods.
All other methods only support one specific protocol version.
Use the
.Em version-flexible
methods instead of the version specific methods.
.Pp
If you want to limit the supported protocols for the version flexible
methods you can use
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_min_proto_version 3 ,
.Xr SSL_set_min_proto_version 3 ,
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_max_proto_version 3
and
.Xr SSL_set_max_proto_version 3
functions.
Using these functions it is possible to choose e.g.
.Fn TLS_server_method
and be able to negotiate with all possible clients, but to only allow
newer protocols like TLS 1.0, TLS 1.1, TLS 1.2 or TLS 1.3.
.Pp
The list of protocols available can also be limited using the
.Sy SSL_OP_NO_SSLv3 ,
.Sy SSL_OP_NO_TLSv1 ,
.Sy SSL_OP_NO_TLSv1_1 ,
.Sy SSL_OP_NO_TLSv1_3 ,
.Sy SSL_OP_NO_TLSv1_2
and
.Sy SSL_OP_NO_TLSv1_3
options of the
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_options 3
or
.Xr SSL_set_options 3
functions, but this approach is not recommended.
Clients should avoid creating "holes" in the set of protocols they
support.
When disabling a protocol, make sure that you also disable either all
previous or all subsequent protocol versions.
In clients, when a protocol version is disabled without disabling
.Em all
previous protocol versions, the effect is to also disable all subsequent
protocol versions.
.Pp
The SSLv3 protocol is deprecated and should generally not be used.
Applications should typically use
.Xr SSL_CTX_set_min_proto_version 3
to set the minimum protocol to at least
.Sy TLS1_VERSION .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The following return values can occur:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It NULL
The creation of a new SSL_CTX object failed.
Check the error stack to find out the reason.
.It Pointer to an SSL_CTX object
The return value points to an allocated SSL_CTX object.
.Pp
.Fn SSL_CTX_up_ref
returns 1 for success and 0 for failure.
.El
